    <entry>
        <title type="html"><![CDATA[Update Safari support for @position-try as it was implemented in Safari 26]]></title>
        <id>https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28017</id>
        <link href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/28017"/>
        <updated>2025-09-28T03:49:47.000Z</updated>
        <content type="html"><![CDATA[<img src="https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/2977353?u=16bc8a352fe2375d06afa25a6b6e3f56bbfa07dd&v=4" width="64" height="64" alt=""/><br/>
<h4 dir="auto">Summary</h4>

<p dir="auto">I believe this was missed in <a class="issue-link js-issue-link" data-error-text="Failed to load title" data-id="3153512050" data-permission-text="Title is private" data-url="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/issues/27087" data-hovercard-type="pull_request" data-hovercard-url="/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27087/hovercard" href="https://github.com/mdn/browser-compat-data/pull/27087">#27087</a>. This was implemented in Safari 26 as part of the anchor positioning work.</p>
<h4 dir="auto">Test results and supporting details</h4>

<p dir="auto">I tested adding a <code class="notranslate">@position-try</code> rule to a CSS file on a website I built and it showed up as a valid rule in Safari 26:</p>
<a target="_blank" rel="noopener noreferrer" href="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/2977353/494816642-d02056a6-9b73-49ee-bfc7-288d8ef00cd6.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..o4OTwZHo_-dGQG9a4iDZ2je0XoiCwUP97aLJhWuPzIU"><img width="1361" height="525" alt="Screenshot 2025-09-27 at 9 28 32 PM" src="https://private-user-images.githubusercontent.com/2977353/494816642-d02056a6-9b73-49ee-bfc7-288d8ef00cd6.png?jwt=eyJ0eXAiOiJKV1QiLCJhbGciOiJIUzI1NiJ9..o4OTwZHo_-dGQG9a4iDZ2je0XoiCwUP97aLJhWuPzIU" style="max-width: 100%; height: auto; max-height: 525px;"></a>

<p dir="auto">See the WPT tests for @position-try in Safari:</p>
<ul dir="auto">
